# Oracle probe (L11.9, ADR 0186) — strings are code points, not bytes (L11.5).
# len("café") is 4 in CPython and 5 in gusty, and "héllo"[1] is "é" rather than the byte 195:
# strings are byte sequences here, not code points. Iterating text used to be a second,
# unrelated defect — the unrolled loop emitted an invalid `store i32 @.str1`, fixed by Gap R.15
# (ADR 0208) — so both backends now run this program and agree on the same wrong answer.
print(len("café"))
print("héllo"[1])
for ch in "aé":
    print(ch)
